{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 SGM Studios Essentials\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A set of REAPER utility scripts I use in my own sessions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each script can be run on its own. Included:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - SGM_route_mix_bus.lua - Route the selected tracks (or all top-level tracks) through a Mix Bus. DRY_RUN preview mode.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - SGM_auto_master.lua - One-click mastering chain on the master bus using ReaEQ, ReaComp and ReaLimit.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - SGM_FieldyBagToggle.lua - Toggle between the Fieldy (FX slots 1-3) and Dimebag (slots 4-6) bass chains.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - SGM_reaper_ultra_hd_smart_tools.lua - Generate a 4K-friendly theme file and optionally start the smart-tool cursor engine.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - daw-discovery-analyzer.lua - Profile your REAPER environment: system, audio device, plugins, routing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - SGM_Utils.lua - Shared utility library available to your own scripts. Not an action; none of the bundled scripts load it automatically.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Fieldy-Bag Toggle\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Toggles between two bass guitar FX chains: Fieldy (slap/rock) and Dimebag (metal). Requires the correct plugin ordering on the selected bass track.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 FX slot layout: slots 1-3 = Fieldy chain (Korn-style slap/rock bass), slots 4-6 = Dimebag chain (Pantera-style metal bass).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 How it works: the state of slot 1 decides which chain is active. If slots 1-3 are enabled the script switches to Dimebag (4-6 on, 1-3 bypassed); run it again to switch back.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 How to use: 1. Select a bass track with FX in slots 1-6. 2. Run the script. 3. The console shows which chain is now active.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Edge cases handled: no track selected shows a message box; a track with no FX reports "No FX found on selected track."; a track with fewer than 4 FX reports that there is nothing to toggle.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 REAPER Auto Mastering Tool\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Applies a mastering chain to the master bus using built-in REAPER plugins (ReaEQ, ReaComp, ReaLimit).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Chain order: 1. ReaEQ high-pass at 30 Hz (removes subsonic rumble). 2. ReaComp bus compression. 3. ReaLimit brickwall limiting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 How to use: run the script. If the master track already has FX you are asked whether to replace them. Answer No or Cancel to leave the project untouched (no undo point is created).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Configuration (edit at top of script): HPF_FREQ = 30 (Hz), COMP_THRESH = -18 (dB), COMP_RATIO = 2 (x:1), LIMIT_CEIL = -1.0 (dBTP).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Edge cases handled: cancelling the dialog changes nothing; a missing stock plug-in is reported and skipped instead of aborting the chain.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 REAPER Ultra HD Smart Tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Generates a 4K/UHD-friendly theme file with a high-contrast, WCAG-checked color palette (dark theme with Pro Tools-inspired blue accents).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 What it does: writes SGM_UltraHD_v<version>.ReaperTheme into your ColorThemes folder, checks the text/background contrast ratio and brightens the primary text colour when it is below the WCAG AAA target (7:1). Optionally starts a context-aware cursor engine modelled on the Pro Tools smart tool.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 How to use: 1. Run the script; it writes the theme file and reports the path. 2. Load it via Options > Themes > Theme (a script cannot switch themes). 3. Answer Yes if you want the smart-tool cursor engine, which requires the SWS extension.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Limitations: the smart-tool engine keeps a defer loop running until the script is terminated from the Actions window. HEAP: the cursor engine only reports the resolved tool in the console; it does not change your mouse modifiers. Some UI elements may need manual tweaking depending on DPI scaling.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 SGM Route Mix Bus\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates (or finds) a dedicated Mix Bus track, disables the master/parent send on the routed tracks and routes them all through the Mix Bus. The Mix Bus itself feeds the Master - useful for bus compression, overall mix glue or stem-style mixing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Features: DRY_RUN mode previews the changes without applying them. With tracks selected only those are routed; with nothing selected every top-level track is routed. Folder parents are left alone because their children already feed them. Tracks that already have a send to the Mix Bus are skipped.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 How to use: 1. Select the tracks to route (or select nothing for "all"). 2. Run the script. 3. Check the console for a routing summary.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Configuration (edit at top of script): MIX_BUS_NAME = "Mix Bus", MIX_BUS_COLOR = \{ r = 255, g = 180, b = 50 \}, DRY_RUN = false, DEBUG = false.\par}
}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 REAPER DAW Discovery and Analyzer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Profiles the current REAPER installation and open project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b What it analyzes:} - Operating system and REAPER version - Audio device configuration (driver, sample rate, block size) - Available plugins (scans installed VST/VST3/AU/JSFX) - Track structure (count, routing graph, folder hierarchy) - Project settings (tempo, time signature, length) - System specs relevant to audio performance (CPU, RAM, disk)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Dependencies:} - Core features work without any external extensions - SWS/S&M Extension enables advanced routing inspection - Script detects SWS availability and adjusts output accordingly\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Output format:} - Clean, formatted console report - Sections: System Info, Audio Config, Plugin Inventory, Track Map, Routing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How to use:} 1. Open a REAPER project 2. Run the script 3. Open View \u8594 ? Console to read the report\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Edge cases handled:} - SWS not installed: routing features limited, note printed in report - Empty project: still reports system info and audio config - No plugins found: reports \u8220"No plugins discovered\u8221"\par}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Rule of 30 Heavy Metal Production Bundle\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A session building system for heavy industrial and metal production in REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Includes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - rule-of-30-session-builder.lua: builds the 48+ track session skeleton (7 sections, folder buses, sidechain routing helper).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - rule-of-30-plugin-presets.lua: plugin chain reference library for Waves / iZotope / FabFilter / Neural DSP / Soundtoys. Shipped for reading and copying; the session builder does not load it at runtime.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 - phase-alignment-tool.lua: transient-based DI guitar alignment with fine nudge controls.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drop Bb tuning. 95-110 BPM. Designed for dense, high-track-count productions with quad-tracked guitars, split bass and augmentation layers.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Phase Alignment Tool\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Analyses the selected guitar DI tracks, detects the first transient in each and nudges the items so they line up with the earliest one - before amp simulation or cabinet processing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Menu: 1 Auto-Align selected tracks, 2 Analyse phase correlation (2 tracks), 3/4 nudge selected items +/-1 ms, 5/6 nudge +/-0.1 ms, 7 show settings.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Settings (edit at top of script): transient_threshold = 0.3, analysis_window = 0.1 s, alignment_precision = 0.0001 s (0.1 ms).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Edge cases handled: fewer than 2 tracks selected, tracks without items, and tracks with no transient above the threshold all exit without touching the project or leaving the UI frozen.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 Courier;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Rule of 30 Session Builder\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Builds a heavy industrial/metal session skeleton: 12-track drum section, 3-band bass split, quad-tracked guitars, vocal layers, glitch/atmosphere and send FX buses. Drop Bb, 100 BPM, project timebase in beats.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Optional plugin inventory: if plugin_inventory.json sits next to the script (or in the REAPER resource folder) its by_category lists are used to choose plug-ins. Expected shape: \{"by_category": \{"EQ": ["ReaEQ"], "Dynamics": ["ReaComp"]\}\}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Compact Mode (menu option 0, default ON): tracks whose category has no matching plug-in are skipped. Turn it off to build the full skeleton with stock FX.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Menu: 0 toggle Compact Mode, 1 build session, 2 drum chains, 3 bass chains, 4 guitar chains, 5 vocal chains, 6 Kick/Bass sidechain routing, 7 close.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The chain presets in rule-of-30-plugin-presets.lua are a reference (Waves / iZotope / FabFilter / Neural DSP / Soundtoys) - the builder does not load that file.\par}
}

